cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the SynapShield exploratory software, cite this repository."
title: "SynapShield: Exploratory reaction-diffusion model for a hypothetical local alpha-synuclein sink"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Owens
    given-names: Steven
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0211-4812
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: https://github.com/artistso/synapshield
    description: Source repository
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-07-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/artistso/synapshield
url: https://github.com/artistso/synapshield
abstract: >-
  SynapShield is research-only software for testing whether a hypothetical
  localized saturable sink can reduce a synthetic one-dimensional concentration
  field under explicit reaction-diffusion assumptions. The software is not a
  medical device, treatment, diagnostic, preventive intervention, clinical
  protocol, or evidence of safety or efficacy. Parameters are not calibrated to
  sufficient experimental data for clinical inference.
keywords:
  - reaction-diffusion
  - numerical modeling
  - alpha-synuclein
  - sensitivity analysis
  - scientific software
  - hypothesis testing
